  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. Ordinary cuts across a bend keep the sheet (mitcad#1628): four L sheets (t=2, r=3, K=0.3, BA=1.8 pi), each a 35 x 20 panel with a 90-degree flange of tangent length 15 (2051.327). (A) An extrusion cuts a 4 mm wide notch through both flanges at the bend (x=-5..10, z=-5..8, y=8..12): its walls are normal to the material everywhere, so the sheet stays valid with the feature's own result (2051.327 - 4 (20 + 4 pi)); its flat pattern has the notch's developed outline (1013.097 - 4 (10 + BA)), and it unfolds and refolds. (B) A rectangle seen from the flange's side (y=48..52, z=1..10) cut through all along x: its bottom wall z=1 runs through the bend at an angle; the cut is made normal to the material from where it leaves the bend's front (outer) surface, with a warning. (C) A 4 mm hole through the flange reaching into the bend likewise. (D) An extrusion joined across the bend adds material: the sheet is invalid, and Unfold names the feature and points to Sheet Cut."},
